WEBVTT

00:28:57.266 --> 00:29:00.980
It does become, essentially, a battle
for power between different tribes.

00:29:01.004 --> 00:29:03.219
DB: Sometimes. But what kind of power?

00:29:03.243 --> 00:29:05.501
The civil rights movement
and Martin Luther King

00:29:05.525 --> 00:29:07.686
and Bayard Rustin and Philip Randolph,

00:29:07.710 --> 00:29:09.380
they believed in the power of love,

00:29:09.404 --> 00:29:11.520
and they believed
in the power of organizing,

00:29:11.544 --> 00:29:13.901
and they believed in the power
of redemptive love.

00:29:13.925 --> 00:29:18.102
King has a famous passage where he says,
you aggressively throw love to the people

00:29:18.126 --> 00:29:19.537
and you love your enemies.

00:29:19.561 --> 00:29:22.100
And at first, they'll hate you
and they'll fight back,

00:29:22.124 --> 00:29:24.894
but eventually, they'll crack
under the power of your love,

00:29:24.918 --> 00:29:27.457
because your power of love
has the power to illuminate

00:29:27.481 --> 00:29:28.864
what's good and what's evil."

00:29:28.888 --> 00:29:30.849
So they believed in that redemptive power